From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:51:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] DSel: frozen cost table and K-stop-aware MTP pricing
 behind G6_S2_DSEL_MODEL=1|2

G6_S2_DSEL_TABLE (inline key:value list or a file; the same on every
rank, its canonical form in the S2 runtime signature) gives the verify
ms by rows 1..8, the drafting ms of a DFlash2 round (d), of an MTP round
(m) and of an MTP chain step (e), a probe's extra (p), and optionally
the MTP rounds' prior under the confidence stop (g, k, n) and the
estimates' prior weight (w). With the model on the drafter choice uses
it in place of DCOST/MCOST/MEACH and spec_len.h's verify table, and
prices an MTP round from its first-position rate, the drafts accepted
after the first and the mean table cost of the request's MTP rounds as
G6_MTP_KSTOP ran them (plus p / probe), not as K drafts. 2: the DFlash2
rounds' own draft count uses the table too. fresh() now keeps the
verify table, decays and prior weight. Off: the steps of before
(checked against the header before this change on 24 configurations).

G6_S2_TIMELINE also prints the mean span per step kind and row count;
tools/s2_dsel_table.py turns a boot's timeline and kstop lines into the
table. Host test batch_dselmodel_test.
