diff --git a/docs/SETTINGS.md b/docs/SETTINGS.md
index 5fbc20e..5535db0 100644
--- a/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@ the short version.
 | `G6_S2_ADAPT` | 0 | S2: choose each round's MTP draft count (1..k) from the sessions' accept rates and the S2 step costs; 1 adds ~1 GiB of main-step graphs |
 | `G6_S2_GROW` | 1 | S2: a session below R holds the KV pages it needs now and takes more as its output grows, admitted and grown only while every live session can still reach prompt + `max_tokens` + guard; a session that cannot grow sits out rounds. 0 = every run holds that worst case from admission |
 | `G6_S2_DSEL` | 1 | S2 with DFlash2: a request that decodes alone drafts each round with DFlash2 or MTP, whichever is expected to commit more tokens per ms (prose +4.5% on RigMark, code level); 0 = DFlash2 every round. `G6_S2_DSEL_MARGIN` (0.15), `G6_S2_DSEL_DWELL` (8 rounds) and `G6_S2_DSEL_PROBE` (4) tune it; `G6_S2_DSEL_DCOST` (8.1), `G6_S2_DSEL_MCOST` (5.5) and `G6_S2_DSEL_MEACH` (2.1) override its drafting ms per round (DFlash2; MTP's first form and the drafter's context step; each MTP chain step) |
+| `G6_S2_DSEL_MODEL` | 0 | S2 drafter choice: 1 = price both drafters from one frozen cost table, `G6_S2_DSEL_TABLE` (a `key:value` list or the path of a file holding one: verify ms by rows `v1`..`v8`, drafting ms `d` (DFlash2 round), `m` (MTP round), `e` (MTP chain step), `p` (a probe's extra), and optionally the MTP rounds' prior under `G6_MTP_KSTOP`: `g` drafts accepted after the first, `k` verified, `n` drafted, and `w` the estimates' prior weight), in place of `G6_S2_DSEL_DCOST`/`_MCOST`/`_MEACH` and the built-in verify table, and price MTP rounds as the confidence stop runs them (their mean table cost and accepted drafts in the request) instead of as `--mtp` drafts; 2 = the DFlash2 rounds' own draft count (`--spec-adaptive`) uses the table too. `tools/s2_dsel_table.py` writes the table from a `G6_S2_TIMELINE` + `G6_MTP_LPLOG` boot. The table is in the S2 runtime signature: every rank must read the same one |
 | `G6_S2_DSEL_START` | dflash | S2 drafter choice: `mtp` = a DFlash2 request starts on MTP (the drafter's prompt-tail drafts are its first probe) and moves to DFlash2 when the evidence says so. Every rank must set the same value |
 | `G6_S2_DSEL_POSCLK` | 0 | S2 drafter choice: 1 = its DFlash2 and MTP estimates decay a draft position only on rounds that observe it, so the DFlash2 rounds (which score MTP's first draft alone) no longer age MTP's later positions toward the seed. Every rank must set the same value |
 | `G6_MTP_KSTOP` | 0 | S2 drafter choice, MTP rounds of a request that decodes alone: 1 = verify draft j while the MTP head's p_1 x .. x p_j >= `G6_MTP_KSTOP_TAU` t_j (default `0,0.2,0.5`; at least one draft) and stop the chain before a draft that could not pass; 2 = choose the count from the drafter choice's MTP estimates (`G6_MTP_KSTOP_SEED3`, 0.55: their prior for a third draft). `G6_MTP_KSTOP_KMAX` (1..3, default `--mtp`) is the most drafts. Drafts only: the target decides every token, but the verify's row count (and so its k1 split class) varies. Every rank must set the same values |
